      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Labeling it an outright myth is extreme, but recognizing its severe structural biases is accurate. While full \"fairness\" might be unattainable under the current model, these organizations still serve vital functions in setting norms, providing humanitarian aid, and acting as crucial forums for dialogue. Their utility lies not in flawless enforcement, but in providing a necessary, albeit flawed, institutional structure to manage global interactions. Any potential for improvement requires significant, difficult reforms regarding representation and accountability.",
      "source": "target",
